<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n89632" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσκομ-ίζω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.115
				</span></i>
			:— <i>carry</i> or <i>convey to</i> a place, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς Σύβοτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.50
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				7.3.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Oec.</u>
				11.16
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθους π</span>., for building,
				<i><span class="en">
				D.
				55.20
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὴν μηχανήν</span>
			<i>bring up</i> the engine to assault the wall, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.115
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς Ἀχαιοῖς π. τὴν πόλιν</span>
			<i>win</i> it to their side, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Arat.</u>
				25
			</span></i>; <i>bring as a gift</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>VH</u>
					1.31
				</span></i>
			:— 
				Med.
			, <i>bring with one, bring home</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.54
			</span></i>; <i>procure</i> necessaries, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				6.1.23
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, of ships, <i>to be brought to</i> a place, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.51
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				5.1.19
			</span></i> (s. v.l.).</div>
